<title>USA: Amcor files shelf for $200 mln in notes.</title>
<headline>Amcor files shelf for $200 mln in notes.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amcor Ltd filed Tuesday a shelf registration with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission for up to $200 million in convertible subordinated perpetual notes.</p>
<p>Net proceeds will be used for general corporate purposes, including repayment of debt, the Australian-based natural resources company said.</p>
<p>The offering will be made through Merrill Lynch &amp; Co and Morgan Stanley &amp; Co Inc. The underwriters have an over-allotment option of up to $30 million of notes.</p>
</text>
